title: "TEECAM: Trusted Execution and Edge Container Anomaly Monitor"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zheng
    given-names: Shenchenyang
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-01"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22234396"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Dokiiiier/TEECAM"
url: "https://github.com/Dokiiiier/TEECAM"
abstract: >-
  TEECAM is a reproducible research prototype for security monitoring in
  containerised edge systems. It combines a narrow gateway to OP-TEE secure
  storage, window-based anomaly detection using percentile and Isolation
  Forest models, and an OP-TEE audit Trusted Application that issues
  HMAC-protected receipts for submitted alert digests.
keywords:
  - trusted execution environment
  - OP-TEE
  - container security
  - anomaly detection
  - Isolation Forest
  - tamper-evident audit
